"Outcome: None\n\nProtocol code:\n\"\"\"\nPyLabRobot Protocol Template\n===========================\n\nThis is the golden template for all PyLabRobot protocols.\nIt provides the necessary scaffolding and structure that every PyLabRobot protocol must have.\n\nThe Agent will replace the [AGENT_CODE_STUB] placeholder with generated protocol logic.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nfrom pylabrobot.liquid_handling import LiquidHandler\nfrom pylabrobot.liquid_handling.backends import (\n    ChatterBoxBackend,  # For simulation\n    # Add other backends as needed\n)\n\n# Import common PyLabRobot resources.\n# Note: Specific resources like plates and tip racks are usually defined in the\n# hardware configuration and loaded dynamically, not imported directly.\nfrom pylabrobot.resources import Plate, TipRack, Well\n\n\nasync def protocol(lh: LiquidHandler):\n    \"\"\"\n    Main protocol function for PyLabRobot.\n\n    This function contains all the liquid handling operations.\n    The AI Agent will replace the placeholder below with generated protocol logic.\n\n    Args:\n        lh (LiquidHandler): The liquid handler instance for performing operations\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # [AGENT_CODE_STUB]\n    \"\"\"\n    PyLabRobot Protocol Template (CORRECTED)\n    ========================================\n\n    Fix applied: Replaced deprecated `ChatterBoxBackend` with\n    `LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend` (per deprecation warning that caused\n    GeneralError: \"ChatterBoxBackend is deprecated. Use\n    LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend instead.\").\n    \"\"\"\n\n    import asyncio\n    from pylabrobot.liquid_handling import LiquidHandler\n\n    # FIXED: LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend is the non-deprecated backend name\n    from pylabrobot.liquid_handling.backends import LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend\n\n    # Import common PyLabRobot resources.\n    from pylabrobot.resources import Plate, TipRack, Well\n\n\n    async def protocol(lh: LiquidHandler):\n    \"\"\"\n    Main protocol function for PyLabRobot.\n\n    Args:\n        lh (LiquidHandler): The liquid handler instance for performing operations\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # ======================================================================\n    # INDEPENDENT REPLICATION EXPERIMENT\n    # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Purpose:\n    #   Reproduce a plate-based sample/reagent assay independently so that\n    #   reported FIGURES (per-sample signals), CLAIMS (reproducibility across\n    #   triplicates; blanks near background) and LIMITATIONS (single-plate\n    #   scope, manual-pipetting bias, reservoir dead volume) can be bound to\n    #   freshly generated data.\n    #\n    # Design:\n    #   - 8 samples   : source_plate column 1 (A1..H1)\n    #   - Triplicates : destination_plate columns 2, 3, 4 (same row)\n    #   - Blanks      : destination_plate column 5 (reagent only)\n    #   - Reagent     : 20 uL per destination well from reagent_trough A1\n    #   - Sample      : 10 uL per replicate (30 uL final in replicate wells)\n    #\n    # Constraints respected:\n    #   - 50 uL tips          -> every aspirate kept <= 20 uL\n    #   - 96 tips available   -> 64 tips used (32 reagent + 24 sample + 8 blank)\n    # ======================================================================\n\n    # ---- 1. Acquire pre-configured deck resources ----\n    tip_rack = lh.get_resource(\"tip_rack_50ul\")\n    source_plate = lh.get_resource(\"source_plate\")\n    dest_plate = lh.get_resource(\"destination_plate\")\n    trough = lh.get_resource(\"reagent_trough\")\n\n    rows = [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\", \"F\", \"G\", \"H\"]\n    rep_columns = [2, 3, 4]        # triplicate columns on destination plate\n    blank_column = 5               # reagent-only negative controls\n    REAGENT_VOL = 20.0             # uL reagent per destination well\n    SAMPLE_VOL = 10.0              # uL sample per replicate\n    MIX_VOL = 15.0                 # uL mixing stroke (below tip capacity)\n    MIX_CYCLES = 3\n\n    # NOTE: ensure channel A1 of the trough holds >= 1.5 mL reagent\n    # (32 wells x 20 uL delivery + 32 x 20 uL pre-wet = ~1.3 mL, plus dead volume).\n\n    # ---- 2. Sequential tip management (column-major through the rack) ----\n    tip_positions = [f\"{r}{c}\" for c in range(1, 13) for r in rows]\n    tips_used = 0\n\n    async def take_tip():\n        \"\"\"Pick the next free tip; fail loudly if the rack is exhausted.\"\"\"\n        nonlocal tips_used\n        if tips_used >= len(tip_positions):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"Tip rack exhausted: replication protocol requires 64 tips.\"\n            )\n        tip_well = tip_rack[tip_positions[tips_used]]\n        tips_used += 1\n        await lh.pick_up_tips(tip_well)\n        return tip_well\n\n    # ---- 3. Reagent addition (20 uL into every replicate + blank well) ----\n    # Pre-wet each fresh tip to minimise droplet loss / first-draw bias,\n    # then deliver reagent to its target well.\n    reagent_well_names = [\n        f\"{r}{c}\" for c in (rep_columns + [blank_column]) for r in rows\n    ]\n    for well_name in reagent_well_names:\n        tip_well = await take_tip()\n        # Pre-wet (aspirate + dispense back into the trough)\n        await lh.aspirate(trough[\"A1\"], vols=[REAGENT_VOL])\n        await lh.dispense(trough[\"A1\"], vols=[REAGENT_VOL])\n        # Deliver reagent\n        await lh.aspirate(trough[\"A1\"], vols=[REAGENT_VOL])\n        await lh.dispense(dest_plate[well_name], vols=[REAGENT_VOL])\n        await lh.drop_tips(tip_well)\n\n    # ---- 4. Sample transfer (10 uL into each triplicate well) ----\n    # Each (row, replicate column) transfer gets a fresh tip to prevent\n    # carry-over that would corrupt cross-sample comparisons (a key claim).\n    for row in rows:\n        for col in rep_columns:\n            tip_well = await take_tip()\n            source_well = source_plate[f\"{row}1\"]\n            dest_well = dest_plate[f\"{row}{col}\"]\n\n            await lh.aspirate(source_well, vols=[SAMPLE_VOL])\n            await lh.dispense(dest_well, vols=[SAMPLE_VOL])\n\n            # Homogenise the 30 uL final volume with a manual up/down mix\n            for _ in range(MIX_CYCLES):\n                await lh.aspirate(dest_well, vols=[MIX_VOL])\n                await lh.dispense(dest_well, vols=[MIX_VOL])\n\n            await lh.drop_tips(tip_well)\n\n    # ---- 5. Mix blank wells (binds the negative-control claim) ----\n    for row in rows:\n        tip_well = await take_tip()\n        blank_well = dest_plate[f\"{row}{blank_column}\"]\n        for _ in range(MIX_CYCLES):\n            await lh.aspirate(blank_well, vols=[MIX_VOL])\n            await lh.dispense(blank_well, vols=[MIX_VOL])\n        await lh.drop_tips(tip_well)\n\n    # ---- 6. Bind-out summary: what this plate supports downstream ----\n    print(\"Replication run complete. Layout produced:\")\n    print(\"  - Triplicate samples : destination cols 2-4 (rows A-H), 30 uL each\")\n    print(\"  - Reagent blanks     : destination col 5 (rows A-H), 20 uL each\")\n    print(\"Binding guidance:\")\n    print(\"  FIGURES  : per-sample triplicate signals -> mean +/- SD plots\")\n    print(\"  CLAIMS   : replicate CV <= 15% ; blanks <= 2x background\")\n    print(\"  LIMITS   : single-plate scope; trough dead volume uncompensated;\")\n    print(\"             no on-deck temperature control/incubation step\")\n    print(f\"Tips consumed: {tips_used} / {len(tip_positions)}\")\n\n    print(\"--- PROTOCOL_SUCCESS ---\")\n\n\n    async def main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main execution function that sets up the liquid handler and runs the protocol.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FIXED: use LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend instead of deprecated ChatterBoxBackend\n    lh = LiquidHandler(backend=LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend(), deck_layout=None)\n\n    try:\n        # Setup the liquid handler\n        await lh.setup()\n\n        # Run the protocol\n        await protocol(lh)\n\n        print(\"✅ Protocol execution completed successfully!\")\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"❌ Protocol execution failed: {e}\")\n        raise\n    finally:\n        # Always stop the liquid handler to clean up resources\n        try:\n            await lh.stop()\n        except Exception as cleanup_error:\n            print(f\"⚠️ Warning: Failed to clean up liquid handler: {cleanup_error}\")\n\n\n    if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    \"\"\"\n    Entry point for running the protocol.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"🚀 Starting PyLabRobot Protocol Execution...\")\n    asyncio.run(main())\n    ```\n\n    **Fix Summary:**\n    - **Root cause:** The `ChatterBoxBackend` class was deprecated in PyLabRobot and raises an exception at import/instantiation time, aborting the protocol before any liquid handling occurred.\n    - **Change 1 (import):** `from pylabrobot.liquid_handling.backends import ChatterBoxBackend` → `from pylabrobot.liquid_handling.backends import LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend`\n    - **Change 2 (instantiation):** `LiquidHandler(backend=ChatterBoxBackend(), ...)` → `LiquidHandler(backend=LiquidHandlerChatterboxBackend(), ...)`\n    - **Protocol logic unchanged:** All pipetting operations, tip management, volumes, and resource accesses were valid and are preserved as-is.\n\nasync def main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main execution function that sets up the liquid handler and runs the protocol.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize the liquid handler with a simulation backend\n    lh = LiquidHandler(backend=ChatterBoxBackend(), deck_layout=None)\n    \n    try:\n        # Setup the liquid handler\n        await lh.setup()\n        \n        # Run the protocol\n        await protocol(lh)\n        \n        print(\"✅ Protocol execution completed successfully!\")\n        \n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"❌ Protocol execution failed: {e}\")\n        raise\n    finally:\n        # Always stop the liquid handler to clean up resources\n       